Provenance
  engine/        The statistics engine of RINK-VT 2.5.0-rinkvt.1, the reference edition (the HERMIT gateway and
                 RINK-VT statistics terminal), by the same author: the command language, frames, game actor,
                 models, roster importer and the HK001 laboratory, as source files, unchanged by this edition
                 except where the reference edition itself changed them for it (a host-kept league), and for
                 the start frame (START) added in 2.5.0-lkvexa.2 and the whistle (WHISTLE) and league overtime
                 rules (rink overtime) added in 2.5.0-lkvexa.3, which keep every earlier behaviour: a game without
                 league rules plays and replays exactly as before. The engine runs in the browser window; none of
                 it needs Node.js.
  engine/rink/hk001/
                 Contains code derived from the Go standard library; its notices and licence terms are kept in
                 engine/rink/hk001/NOTICE.md and continue to apply to those parts.
  photon/        The Photon host follows the design of VEC1 Photon (Design Photon 0.6.0, Generic Photon 0.2.0,
                 WindowsSafe-r1, Copyright 2026 RUSSELL PHILIP SMITHSON, GPL-3.0-only): a control plane, a
                 Chromium-family renderer window on an isolated profile, a loopback JSON API guarded by Host,
                 Origin and a per-launch token, and a release-integrity gate. Where VEC1 Photon's control plane is
                 a Python program, this edition's is a native program written in Go with its standard library
                 only (photon/*.go). No Photon source file is copied. From 2.5.0-lkvexa.4 there is no Python and
                 no Node.js anywhere in the edition: nothing has to be installed to run, verify or document it.
  photon/bin/    The host for each platform, built from photon/*.go (photon/build.cmd, photon/build.sh). Each
                 executable contains the Go runtime and standard library, Copyright 2009 The Go Authors, under the
                 BSD 3-Clause licence whose text is in photon/LICENSE-GO; that licence applies to those parts.
  contracts/     MSSL 0.3 records in the observed subset described by the MSSL Writers Corpus 1.0.0, and JA Core
                 0.3 contract sources in the provisional grammar of the JA21 JA Core Application Language Suite
                 1.0.0 (both Copyright 2026 RUSSELL PHILIP SMITHSON, GPL-3.0-only). Neither corpus is bundled.
                 The JA sources are modeled contracts: no JA Core parser, compiler or VM is supplied or claimed.
                 The records are written and checked by the host's own contracts command, which applies the
                 single-document rules of the corpus validator; the validator itself is not part of the edition.

Data
  The four demonstration clubs and every simulated game are fictional. HK001 is a deterministic synthetic
  research laboratory; it gives no forecasts, odds, or roster, medical, scouting or officiating advice.

